  "faq": [
    {
      "q": "What is a .gitignore file?",
      "a": "It tells git which files and folders to ignore, so build output, dependencies and secrets are never committed to your repository."
    },
    {
      "q": "Can I combine presets?",
      "a": "Yes — that is the point. A Node.js project on macOS, for example, ticks Node.js + macOS, and both rule sets are merged with headers."
    },
    {
      "q": "Is .gitignore enough to protect secrets?",
      "a": "It prevents accidental commits going forward, but once a secret is committed it stays in history. Use it alongside rotating any credentials you have already pushed."
    },
    {
      "q": "Is the file uploaded anywhere?",
      "a": "No. It is generated locally in your browser."
    }
  ]
